Key Clarifications
- Why d_lookup can return NULL: it is a cache lookup only; first random name usually not cached.
- Why d_alloc_parallel after NULL: creates/race-resolves dentry candidate so filesystem lookup can proceed safely.
- Is IS_ERR(dentry) from d_alloc_parallel expected for missing file: NO; ENOENT is semantic missing-file result later, IS_ERR here is hard failure (e.g., -ENOMEM).
- Where missing-file decision is made in this path: atomic_open negative check at fs/namei.c:3592 then error=-ENOENT at 3593.

